---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Accessibility Statement — TH Homes" description="TH Homes' commitment to an accessible and inclusive website.">
  <section class="page-hero legal-hero"><div class="page-hero-inner"><h1>Designed to include.</h1><p>Our commitment to making the TH Homes website clear, usable and accessible to as many people as possible.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><article class="section-inner legal-copy">
    <p class="legal-updated">Last reviewed: 23 November 2026</p>
    <h2>Our approach</h2><p>TH Homes aims to provide equal access to its digital information and services. Our approach is informed by the Discrimination Against Persons with Disabilities (Prohibition) Act 2018 and the internationally recognised Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 Level AA.</p>
    <h2>What the website supports</h2><ul><li>Keyboard navigation and visible focus indicators</li><li>Semantic headings, labels and descriptive alternative text</li><li>Responsive layouts that work on mobile and desktop</li><li>Text resizing and browser zoom</li><li>Reduced motion preferences and paused ambient video when reduced motion is requested</li><li>Light and dark appearance choices with readable contrast</li></ul>
    <h2>Known limitations</h2><p>Some third-party or legacy media may not yet include complete audio description or captions. We are reviewing media and will provide an accessible alternative on request while improvements are made.</p>
    <h2>Tell us about a barrier</h2><p>If you cannot access information or complete a task, please use our <a href="/contact">contact page</a> and describe the page, the barrier and the format you need. We will acknowledge the issue and work to provide an accessible alternative. Verified accessibility contact details and response targets must be added before launch.</p>
    <p class="legal-note">Accessibility is an ongoing practice. We test changes across keyboard, touch, responsive layouts and reduced-motion settings, and will review this statement as the website evolves.</p>
  </article></section>
</BaseLayout>
